The AMP Challenge 2027 submission contract and reference validator are defined
by szczurek-lab/amp-challenge-2027, distributed under BSD-3-Clause.

DRAMP data downloaded from https://dramp.cpu-bioinfor.org/ on 2026-09-03 are
used under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0. The patent peptide dataset is not
included. Source file hashes and retrieval URLs are recorded in
configs/data_sources.json.

The APEX pathogen inference repository and pretrained weights are referenced at
commit 417a4441a1e6ef8b10d2352e1c059622d5259f3a under its MIT license. They are
not redistributed by this repository, and APEX training observations are not
represented as part of the DRAMP-derived dataset.

The frozen representation is facebook/esm2_t12_35M_UR50D, pinned at revision
6fbf070e65b0b7291e7bbcd451118c216cff79d8 under its MIT license. No backbone
weights are redistributed. The committed `esm2-mic16-v2.json` contains only fitted
logistic-ridge coefficients, scalers, calibration parameters, and provenance hashes.

The committed `linear-physchem-v1.json` checkpoint was trained locally from the
pinned DRAMP-derived tables. It contains only fitted scalar coefficients,
calibration parameters, metrics, and content hashes; it does not redistribute
the source workbook.

This project does not claim that its bootstrap heuristic generator is a
competitive biological model. It exists to exercise the complete, deterministic
submission path while learned generators and calibrated oracles are developed.
